  "schema": 1,
  "note": "Class archetypes — the engineering starting position a car of this class inherits when no real GT7 data has been captured for it. UAT 2026-08-07 defect A1/A7. Each parameter carries a preference WINDOW (the band a competent engineer works inside for this class), an ANCHOR (the class-typical starting value), and a STEP. The archetype deliberately does NOT declare a legal min/max: GT7's actual slider limits are unknown for every car in the repository, and inventing them would be exactly the failure this file exists to correct. Legal bounds stay with strategy.setup_ranges.GENERIC_DEFAULTS (the outer safety clamp) until a real per-car capture lands in data/car_gt7_ranges.json, which overrides everything here field by field. Anchors and windows are calibrated from evidence already on disk — see each archetype's 'source' — not invented. Springs are GT7's natural-frequency slider (Hz), which reads far lower than real-world suspension frequency: a Gr.3 sits near 3.0-5.0 here, not the 4.5-6.5 a real GT3 runs. Camber and toe use the positive convention (toe negative = toe-OUT). Drivetrain shaping of these anchors is NOT applied here — it belongs to strategy.setup_anchor, which layers RR/FR/FF/MR/4WD adjustments on top of the class position.",
  "step_note": "Steps are the app's existing field precision (strategy.setup_baseline._round_for_field), NOT observed GT7 increments. They are marked tier 'assumed' by the loader and are replaced wholesale by a real capture. Do not treat them as GT7 truth.",
